# mix-of-capabilities 04 (ricordare) — dopo la lettura, «what is X?» risponde con la
# definizione letta (topic_definition, con l'indirizzo in topic_read), non con la
# classe estratta ne' con «I have no definition of it, but I read». Le letture sono
# vere e salvate (Wikipedia: Fire blanket, Smoke detector, Thermal runaway).
[mock live]
!set PARROT0_SESSION=
!set PARROT0_PROFILE=kb/profiles/agi.p0
!set PARROT0_LANG=en
!reset

[test the read definition answers, also for a compound name after an article]
!timeout 30
!query topic_read(fire_blanket, wiki_address(en, "Fire blanket", $R, lead))
> what is a fire blanket?
<~ A fire blanket is a safety device designed to extinguish incipient (starting) fires.
<! classed as
> what is a smoke detector?
<~ senses smoke, typically as an indicator of fire
> what is thermal runaway?
<~ accelerated by increased temperature
<! I have no definition of it

[test asked for the source, the answer cites the read address and says it is read text]
!timeout 30
> what is a fire blanket?
> where did you read that?
<~ I read it on Wikipedia: the article «Fire blanket» (en edition, revision
<~ not a conclusion of mine
> what is thermal runaway?
> what is your source?
<~ the article «Thermal runaway»
<! came from Rome
